Run a command over SSH as the Machine's resolved identity; confirm or refuse an unproved host key and return the client's exit status. The session runs as the identity the Machine's desired state authorizes, over a host key proved before any credential is offered; an unproved key is confirmed interactively or refused. The exit status is the client's. Bootwright flags go before the command. Use -- before a flag-shaped first payload value to preserve it as data. After the first payload value, all remaining tokens belong to the payload.

Usage:
  bootwright machine exec <command>... [flags]

Examples:
  bootwright machine exec --context lab --name node -- uname -a

Flags:
      --name string   Select the exact object name (required)

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines
